Quiet!

276
00:11:09,708 --> 00:11:11,166
Let me see what he says!

277
00:11:20,208 --> 00:11:21,833
This baker's apprentice,

278
00:11:21,875 --> 00:11:23,208
Was he sure?

279
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:25,333
Didn't you go see if it's true?

280
00:11:26,375 --> 00:11:28,125
May it never happen to you, Sir!

281
00:11:29,083 --> 00:11:30,958
We went to Shir-Ali's shop

282
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,458
To ask if it's true or not.

283
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:33,125
Well?

284
00:11:33,458 --> 00:11:36,333
The moment the wretch heard Mr. Asdollah-Mirza's name,

285
00:11:36,375 --> 00:11:37,750
Let out a roar,

286
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:39,791
Like a bellowing buffalo!

287
00:11:40,625 --> 00:11:41,875
He said, who told you?

288
00:11:42,291 --> 00:11:43,458
We told him nothing!

289
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,750
The wretch chased us with a leg of lamb!

290
00:11:46,791 --> 00:11:47,250
Ugh!

291
00:11:47,583 --> 00:11:49,291
We got scared and told him.

292
00:11:49,541 --> 00:11:50,541
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie!

293
00:11:50,541 --> 00:11:52,166
The grave is this close...

294
00:11:52,375 --> 00:11:53,708
The dough-kneader told me!

295
00:11:53,958 --> 00:11:55,083
We had two legs,

296
00:11:55,291 --> 00:11:57,833
And borrowed two more from God knows where,

297
00:11:57,916 --> 00:11:58,916
We ran home like the wind!

298
00:11:58,958 --> 00:12:00,750
Oh, what a disaster!

299
00:12:02,541 --> 00:12:04,875
Now he probably went after the poor dough-kneader!

300
00:12:05,458 --> 00:12:06,708
No lady!

301
00:12:06,916 --> 00:12:09,166
Then we ran into the dough-kneader in the tree-lined alley,

302
00:12:09,208 --> 00:12:11,625
We told him to stay away from Shir-Ali's shop!

303
00:12:12,208 --> 00:12:13,833
Now, we did talk to the dough-kneader,

304
00:12:13,833 --> 00:12:14,791
Don't think for a moment,

305
00:12:14,791 --> 00:12:16,000
That we want to make up with him!

306
00:12:16,250 --> 00:12:17,750
Sir, think of something!

307
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:18,916
Someone has to

308
00:12:18,916 --> 00:12:20,291
Tell this idiot boy,

309
00:12:20,291 --> 00:12:21,958
To come out of Shir-Ali's house!

310
00:12:22,541 --> 00:12:24,833
Our family's long-standing reputation

311
00:12:24,958 --> 00:12:27,541
Is being ruined by this shameless Asdollah!

312
00:12:27,666 --> 00:12:30,500
A respectable prince going to a butcher's house!

313
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:31,916
I swear,

314
00:12:31,916 --> 00:12:34,500
I'm no man if I don't kill this brazen bastard!

315
00:12:34,708 --> 00:12:35,916
This home-wrecker!

316
00:12:36,125 --> 00:12:37,125
Oh, come on! - Quiet!

317
00:12:39,333 --> 00:12:41,125
Your own honor is intact!

318
00:12:41,791 --> 00:12:44,958
Why fuss over Shir-Ali the butcher's honor?

319
00:12:45,208 --> 00:12:48,333
I'm worried about our family's reputation!

320
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:50,250
For the neighborhood's reputation!

321
00:12:50,541 --> 00:12:54,000
One of our family, in a butcher's house!

322
00:12:54,375 --> 00:12:57,958
A symbol of this country's aristocracy,

323
00:12:58,166 --> 00:12:59,625
In Shir-Ali's house!

324
00:12:59,625 --> 00:13:01,916
And with a young woman!

325
00:13:02,541 --> 00:13:04,916
If I had found him last night!

326
00:13:05,166 --> 00:13:07,000
Shameless lowlife!

327
00:13:07,375 --> 00:13:08,666
Enough Sir!

328
00:13:08,666 --> 00:13:09,291
Enough already!

329
00:13:09,333 --> 00:13:11,416
Don't insult my brother so much!

330
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:14,041
Because of you, he went to a butcher's house

331
00:13:14,083 --> 00:13:15,375
And is staging a sit-in!

332
00:13:15,791 --> 00:13:18,875
I suggest a committee of volunteers

333
00:13:19,333 --> 00:13:21,666
Go negotiate with Asdollah,

334
00:13:21,750 --> 00:13:25,000
And reassure him about this gentleman!

335
00:13:25,125 --> 00:13:26,916
Maybe he'll end his sit-in!

336
00:13:26,958 --> 00:13:28,166
I'll go, Sir!

337
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:30,750
Give me a gun, Sir, I'll go!

338
00:13:32,333 --> 00:13:33,458
I'll go, brother.

339
00:13:33,541 --> 00:13:34,458
Quiet!

340
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:36,125
You don't need to go!

341
00:13:46,083 --> 00:13:47,958
All of you go home.

342
00:13:48,666 --> 00:13:49,791
I'll go myself.

343
00:13:50,208 --> 00:13:52,083
It's not right for you to go, brother!

344
00:13:52,125 --> 00:13:54,333
On the contrary, it's very right!

345
00:13:54,916 --> 00:13:59,583
Because a neutral and impartial person must go!

346
00:14:00,041 --> 00:14:00,916
Brother!

347
00:14:01,208 --> 00:14:03,708
It's not befitting you to go to a butcher's house.

348
00:14:03,708 --> 00:14:08,333
I said a neutral and impartial person must go.

349
00:14:09,041 --> 00:14:10,250
Come Ghasem.

350
00:14:10,583 --> 00:14:11,208
Yes Sir!

351
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:14,041
Come show me Shir-Ali's house.

352
00:14:14,583 --> 00:14:15,375
Lead the way.

353
00:14:15,958 --> 00:14:17,583
Before he gets back,

354
00:14:17,625 --> 00:14:21,708
I must talk with this idiot Asdollah.

355
00:14:31,208 --> 00:14:34,416
The late Roknoddin-Mirza, God rest his soul,

356
00:14:34,750 --> 00:14:37,291
Fathering this child in his old age,

357
00:14:37,375 --> 00:14:39,708
Disgraced a whole family!

358
00:14:40,625 --> 00:14:42,750
And with his gardener's daughter!

359
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,833
Please leave the dead out of this.

360
00:14:46,083 --> 00:14:48,000
What has my late father got to do with it!

361
00:14:48,125 --> 00:14:50,041
The dead have plenty to do with us!

362
00:14:50,125 --> 00:14:52,666
They only get the living into trouble!

363
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,291
If your late father

364
00:14:54,333 --> 00:14:56,458
Hadn't had such a loose waistband,

365
00:14:56,458 --> 00:14:58,625
And hadn't fathered this Prince Asdollah-Mirza,

366
00:14:58,875 --> 00:15:00,166
Would the sky have fallen?

367
00:15:00,291 --> 00:15:02,875
If he hadn't set this wolf on people's families,

368
00:15:02,958 --> 00:15:04,333
Would the world have ended?

369
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,375
Please Mr. Dustali Khan!

370
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:08,625
You of all people

371
00:15:08,625 --> 00:15:09,875
Shouldn't talk about loose waistbands!

372
00:15:10,375 --> 00:15:11,666
Lady Aziz-Saltaneh!

373
00:15:11,708 --> 00:15:12,708
That kitchen knife

374
00:15:12,750 --> 00:15:14,541
To cut off my you-know-what,

375
00:15:14,583 --> 00:15:15,833
Who brought it into bed?

376
00:15:15,875 --> 00:15:16,625
Oh, get away!

377
00:15:20,583 --> 00:15:21,500
Goodbye.

378
00:15:21,625 --> 00:15:22,625
Take care.

379
00:15:22,666 --> 00:15:23,875
I have greens...

380
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,375
Radish root...

381
00:15:25,416 --> 00:15:26,958
Mint, tarragon...

382
00:15:27,416 --> 00:15:28,833
I have greens...

383
00:15:29,083 --> 00:15:31,916
Radish root, mint, tarragon...

384
00:15:32,666 --> 00:15:36,208
Spring greens, wow! Mint, tarragon...

385
00:15:47,625 --> 00:15:48,583
Peace be upon you Sir.

386
00:15:48,666 --> 00:15:50,500
Peace be upon you. - Please pray for me!

387
00:15:50,625 --> 00:15:52,000
I need your prayers...

388
00:15:55,958 --> 00:15:56,541
Sir!

389
00:15:56,791 --> 00:15:58,041
Yes! What is it?

390
00:15:58,083 --> 00:15:59,166
This way, please.

391
00:16:09,208 --> 00:16:10,791
(Knocking on door)

392
00:16:16,208 --> 00:16:18,500
(Knocking on door)

393
00:16:27,208 --> 00:16:27,958
Who is it?

394
00:16:28,583 --> 00:16:30,250
Lady, open the door.

395
00:16:31,125 --> 00:16:32,625
Who are you? What do you want?

396
00:16:33,541 --> 00:16:34,166
Lady!

397
00:16:34,416 --> 00:16:37,875
Is Mr. Shir-Ali at home?

398
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,083
No, he's not.

399
00:16:39,291 --> 00:16:40,416
He went to the shop.

400
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:41,666
Lady!

401
00:16:41,833 --> 00:16:43,041
Please,

402
00:16:43,083 --> 00:16:45,750
Tell Asdollah-Mirza to come to the door.

403
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:47,500
Who?

404
00:16:48,166 --> 00:16:49,791
We don't have such a person here!

405
00:16:50,958 --> 00:16:51,875
Yes, dear... - Is it for me?

406
00:16:51,916 --> 00:16:54,083
Tell him to come to the door! - Say I'm not here! Not here!

407
00:16:54,666 --> 00:16:55,958
Sir, how many times do I have to say it?

408
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,625
We don't have such a person here!

409
00:16:57,833 --> 00:16:59,916
If it's Shir-Ali you want, go to the shop.

410
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:01,625
Dear lady!

411
00:17:01,625 --> 00:17:03,083
Please!

412
00:17:03,125 --> 00:17:04,125
Listen!

413
00:17:04,541 --> 00:17:07,833
We know Asdollah is hiding here!

414
00:17:07,875 --> 00:17:08,291
Yes!

415
00:17:08,291 --> 00:17:10,125
It's important!

416
00:17:10,708 --> 00:17:11,625
If he doesn't come,

417
00:17:11,666 --> 00:17:13,500
It will end badly for him! - Yes! Yes!

418
00:17:13,750 --> 00:17:15,041
His life

419
00:17:15,083 --> 00:17:16,000
Is at stake! - Yes!

420
00:17:16,541 --> 00:17:18,125
Tell him not to be afraid.

421
00:17:18,166 --> 00:17:19,333
We have his back!

422
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:25,083
Come!

423
00:17:25,291 --> 00:17:26,250
It's for you!

424
00:17:26,291 --> 00:17:27,000
Who is it? Ugh!

425
00:17:28,291 --> 00:17:29,125
Wait, I'm coming!

426
00:17:33,291 --> 00:17:35,666
Whoever it is, say I'm not here!

427
00:17:35,750 --> 00:17:36,125
Ugh!

428
00:17:36,416 --> 00:17:37,416
Say I'm not here!

429
00:17:37,416 --> 00:17:38,583
It's your relatives!

430
00:17:38,625 --> 00:17:38,958
Me?

431
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,041
They are not my relatives!

432
00:17:40,083 --> 00:17:41,000
I'm not here!

433
00:17:42,916 --> 00:17:44,458
You don't know... you don't know who it is? You don't know?

434
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:45,208
Moment!

435
00:17:46,708 --> 00:17:47,958
What do you want with me?

436
00:17:48,083 --> 00:17:49,583
What... what do you want from me?

437
00:17:50,416 --> 00:17:51,166
It's him!

438
00:17:51,166 --> 00:17:52,125
Asdollah!

439
00:17:52,166 --> 00:17:53,166
Open the door,

440
00:17:53,208 --> 00:17:54,750
I want to talk to you!

441
00:17:55,166 --> 00:17:56,583
Mo... Moment!

442
00:17:56,666 --> 00:17:58,083
Sir! It's you?

443
00:17:58,166 --> 00:17:59,583
How are you Sir?

444
00:18:00,291 --> 00:18:02,833
Thanks to you, Sir is not well.

445
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,125
Then why don't you open the door Asdollah!

446
00:18:09,166 --> 00:18:10,625
I don't dare Sir!

447
00:18:10,791 --> 00:18:12,250
No one can guarantee my safety!

448
00:18:12,625 --> 00:18:13,791
My life is in danger!

449
00:18:14,125 --> 00:18:15,125
That demonic killer

450
00:18:15,166 --> 00:18:16,583
Is searching door to door for me,

451
00:18:16,583 --> 00:18:17,500
To kill me!

452
00:18:19,416 --> 00:18:20,666
Asdollah!

453
00:18:21,166 --> 00:18:23,291
You're scared for no reason!

454
00:18:23,625 --> 00:18:25,083
I promise you,

455
00:18:25,083 --> 00:18:27,250
It was a misunderstanding, and it's over!

456
00:18:27,291 --> 00:18:27,750
Yes...

457
00:18:27,833 --> 00:18:29,791
Dustali has promised me too

458
00:18:29,833 --> 00:18:32,708
To drop the whole thing and forget it!

459
00:18:32,791 --> 00:18:34,333
Moment! Moment!

460
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:34,708
You,

461
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:36,958
Believe the promise of this wild jackass?

462
00:18:39,166 --> 00:18:40,041
Asdollah!

463
00:18:40,166 --> 00:18:42,875
I give you my word of honor!

464
00:18:42,916 --> 00:18:43,958
Sir I am scared!

465
00:18:44,208 --> 00:18:46,625
First throw that wild jackass in prison...

466
00:18:47,666 --> 00:18:48,916
Asdollah!

467
00:18:49,083 --> 00:18:50,583
I'm telling you, open the door!

468
00:18:50,625 --> 00:18:52,208
I command you!

469
00:18:52,500 --> 00:18:55,000
Sir! I don't want to disobey your order!

470
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,166
But what can I do?

471
00:18:56,208 --> 00:18:57,333
My life is in danger!

472
00:18:57,958 --> 00:19:00,041
I know that from this wild jackass

473
00:19:00,208 --> 00:19:01,625
There is no escape for me!

474
00:19:03,333 --> 00:19:05,500
I am only one step away from death...

475
00:19:06,041 --> 00:19:07,958
I have only a few hours left to live!

476
00:19:08,416 --> 00:19:10,000
Tell all the relatives,

477
00:19:10,041 --> 00:19:11,666
For any good or bad they had from me,

478
00:19:11,666 --> 00:19:12,625
To forgive me!

479
00:19:13,250 --> 00:19:14,416
Tell my brother Shamsali

480
00:19:14,458 --> 00:19:15,541
I'll write my will

481
00:19:15,583 --> 00:19:17,583
And give it to Shir-Ali... (Crying)

482
00:19:19,458 --> 00:19:21,333
Sir, seems a snake bit him somewhere!

483
00:19:21,416 --> 00:19:23,375
Mr. Asdollah-Mirza open the door!

484
00:19:23,458 --> 00:19:24,458
Asdollah!

485
00:19:24,625 --> 00:19:25,583
You idiot!

486
00:19:25,583 --> 00:19:27,083
Hurry up, open the door!

487
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:27,916
Open!

488
00:19:27,916 --> 00:19:29,166
Mr. Asdollah-Mirza!

489
00:19:29,625 --> 00:19:31,291
Have you no mercy!

490
00:19:32,375 --> 00:19:34,291
If you saw my face,

491
00:19:34,333 --> 00:19:35,333
You wouldn't recognize me!

492
00:19:35,458 --> 00:19:36,750
From fear of death,

493
00:19:37,166 --> 00:19:39,083
I aged 20 years in one night!

494
00:19:40,125 --> 00:19:40,833
Tell my brother,

495
00:19:40,833 --> 00:19:41,750
Tell Shamsali,

496
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:43,000
We'll meet again on Judgment Day!

497
00:19:43,583 --> 00:19:46,083
Tell him there's no need to take revenge for me!

498
00:19:46,416 --> 00:19:48,083
I'm tired of it all.

499
00:19:48,708 --> 00:19:50,250
I've thought of a way myself

500
00:19:50,583 --> 00:19:52,333
To save Dustali the trouble.

501
00:19:52,833 --> 00:19:54,541
I will take opium and kill myself,

502
00:19:54,583 --> 00:19:57,250
So they don't throw that poor wretch in prison...

503
00:19:57,333 --> 00:19:59,666
To hell with you and your face!

504
00:19:59,708 --> 00:20:00,291
Open the door! - To hell with your own face,

505
00:20:00,333 --> 00:20:02,250
Open the door!

506
00:20:02,291 --> 00:20:03,833
And your brother!

507
00:20:03,916 --> 00:20:05,333
Shameless bastards!

508
00:20:05,458 --> 00:20:07,875
Ghasem, come on, let's go!

509
00:20:08,125 --> 00:20:08,625
Come!

510
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:10,333
Come!

511
00:20:10,375 --> 00:20:12,375
(Sound of Asdollah-Mirza crying)

512
00:20:48,833 --> 00:20:49,791
What happened, brother?

513
00:20:49,958 --> 00:20:53,416
I talked to him in every language I could think of,

514
00:20:53,583 --> 00:20:55,083
He wouldn't be convinced no matter what!

515
00:20:55,083 --> 00:20:55,791
Brother!

516
00:20:55,916 --> 00:20:57,583
We can't just leave him there like that!

517
00:20:57,583 --> 00:21:00,750
The only way to get him out is,

518
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,833
To send for Shir-Ali the butcher!

519
00:21:03,875 --> 00:21:05,083
And tell him

520
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:07,000
That Asdollah staying

521
00:21:07,208 --> 00:21:09,000
In his house

522
00:21:09,208 --> 00:21:10,875
Is not a good idea!

523
00:21:10,916 --> 00:21:12,625
People will talk!

524
00:21:12,625 --> 00:21:14,458
Yes, yes! That's not a bad idea!

525
00:21:14,708 --> 00:21:17,583
Who dares to say something to Shir-Ali?

526
00:21:17,625 --> 00:21:18,791
Me, Sir me!

527
00:21:18,916 --> 00:21:20,458
You send for Shir-Ali,

528
00:21:20,500 --> 00:21:21,416
I will tell him!

529
00:21:21,791 --> 00:21:22,416
You!

530
00:21:22,541 --> 00:21:23,166
Yes, me!

531
00:21:23,791 --> 00:21:25,458
I've sent for Shir-Ali.

532
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:27,166
When he comes, you tell him!

533
00:21:27,375 --> 00:21:28,125
Me tell him?!

534
00:21:30,083 --> 00:21:31,916
What happened Ghasem? Where is Shir-Ali?

535
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:33,625
God works in mysterious ways!

536
00:21:33,666 --> 00:21:36,458
Nothing in this world goes unpunished!

537
00:21:36,583 --> 00:21:37,958
What happened Ghasem?

538
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,083
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie!

539
00:21:39,125 --> 00:21:40,750
The grave is this close...

540
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,333
His shop was closed!

541
00:21:42,666 --> 00:21:43,750
He got into a fight...

542
00:21:43,750 --> 00:21:44,833
Shir-Ali got into a fight?

543
00:21:45,041 --> 00:21:46,166
Who with?

544
00:21:46,750 --> 00:21:47,666
Well, honestly...

545
00:21:47,875 --> 00:21:49,375
The dough-kneader told the baker,

546
00:21:49,416 --> 00:21:51,416
Mr. Asdollah-Mirza is in Mr. Shir-Ali's house!

547
00:21:51,416 --> 00:21:51,708
Well?

548
00:21:52,208 --> 00:21:55,166
And the baker made a crack at Mr. Shir-Ali.

549
00:21:55,375 --> 00:21:56,333
So Mr. Shir-Ali,

550
00:21:56,333 --> 00:21:57,375
With a leg of lamb,

551
00:21:57,416 --> 00:21:59,375
Hit the dough-kneader on the back of the head!

552
00:21:59,375 --> 00:22:00,333
The baker fainted!

553
00:22:01,125 --> 00:22:02,916
They took the dough-kneader to the hospital.

554
00:22:02,958 --> 00:22:05,333
Now the officers took Shir-Ali to the police station!

555
00:22:05,416 --> 00:22:06,250
Police station!

556
00:22:06,458 --> 00:22:08,125
They took Shir-Ali to the police station?

557
00:22:08,333 --> 00:22:10,458
Did you find out how long they'll keep him?

558
00:22:10,458 --> 00:22:11,791
If Shir-Ali goes to jail,

559
00:22:11,833 --> 00:22:12,541
Perhaps,

560
00:22:12,625 --> 00:22:13,583
Ten days,

561
00:22:13,666 --> 00:22:14,500
Twenty days,

562
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:16,041
Six months, they'll keep him in there!

563
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:18,041
Sir, think of something!

564
00:22:18,208 --> 00:22:19,666
Oh, what a disaster!

565
00:22:19,666 --> 00:22:21,000
Now what's going on?

566
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,791
Why are you shouting so much?

567
00:22:22,791 --> 00:22:24,833
Since when is Shir-Ali so dear to you?

568
00:22:25,791 --> 00:22:28,541
Oh! The police are such a nightmare!

569
00:22:28,541 --> 00:22:29,666
If you press charges,

570
00:22:29,708 --> 00:22:30,416
You're in trouble!

571
00:22:30,458 --> 00:22:31,500
If you drop them,

572
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:32,541
You're in trouble!

573
00:22:32,666 --> 00:22:34,666
You have no idea what I went through

574
00:22:34,791 --> 00:22:36,541
To get this idiot Nayeb Teymoor-Khan

575
00:22:36,583 --> 00:22:37,458
To shelve the case! - Have you heard or not!

576
00:22:37,458 --> 00:22:38,708
They took Shir-Ali the butcher!

577
00:22:38,916 --> 00:22:39,625
All the better!

578
00:22:39,833 --> 00:22:42,000
To hell with him and his rotten meat!

579
00:22:42,041 --> 00:22:43,333
Wake up!

580
00:22:43,875 --> 00:22:46,833
That home-wrecker is in Shir-Ali's house!

581
00:22:47,041 --> 00:22:48,833
That lowlife prince!

582
00:22:48,833 --> 00:22:49,416
What?

583
00:22:49,500 --> 00:22:50,208
Asdollah!

584
00:22:50,625 --> 00:22:52,291
Is that hussy there too?

585
00:22:52,583 --> 00:22:54,666
That hussy tricked the boy!

586
00:22:54,666 --> 00:22:55,708
She snared him!

587
00:22:55,750 --> 00:22:57,250
And you're just sitting there?

588
00:22:57,500 --> 00:22:59,666
Asdollah is captive in Shir-Ali the butcher's house,

589
00:22:59,916 --> 00:23:01,250
And you're doing nothing?

590
00:23:01,791 --> 00:23:03,166
What if that lowlife woman

591
00:23:03,208 --> 00:23:04,791
Has poisoned him!

592
00:23:05,208 --> 00:23:07,750
Lady, don't get angry.

593
00:23:07,958 --> 00:23:11,791
I've just come from Shir-Ali's house myself.

594
00:23:12,166 --> 00:23:15,458
I talked to Asdollah from behind the door!

595
00:23:16,041 --> 00:23:18,250
He just wouldn't come out!

596
00:23:18,625 --> 00:23:20,166
No matter how much I begged,

597
00:23:20,333 --> 00:23:22,125
No matter how much I shouted...

598
00:23:22,166 --> 00:23:23,416
Why? What did he say?

599
00:23:23,416 --> 00:23:24,333
What do I know!

600
00:23:24,333 --> 00:23:25,208
Nonsense!

601
00:23:25,250 --> 00:23:26,166
Rubbish!

602
00:23:26,208 --> 00:23:29,041
He says I'm afraid of Dustali!

603
00:23:29,041 --> 00:23:30,916
I don't dare come out!

604
00:23:30,958 --> 00:23:32,125
What? Dustali!

605
00:23:32,708 --> 00:23:34,041
Who does that dog Dustali think he is,

606
00:23:34,041 --> 00:23:35,791
Laying a hand on my nephew!

607
00:23:35,916 --> 00:23:36,958
I must go myself!

608
00:23:37,166 --> 00:23:38,166
I must go and see

609
00:23:38,208 --> 00:23:39,750
What he's doing in Shir-Ali's house!

610
00:23:40,083 --> 00:23:41,750
That ugly-faced woman

611
00:23:41,958 --> 00:23:43,166
Has bewitched the boy!

612
00:23:43,375 --> 00:23:44,708
She must have bewitched him!

613
00:23:44,750 --> 00:23:45,791
Otherwise he wouldn't stay there!

614
00:23:45,833 --> 00:23:48,041
She probably wants to be bewitched herself!

615
00:23:48,875 --> 00:23:50,791
Why are you talking so much?

616
00:23:51,083 --> 00:23:53,458
She might do something to him!

617
00:23:54,166 --> 00:23:55,416
The lady is right!

618
00:23:56,041 --> 00:23:58,958
We heard Mr. Asdollah-Khan's voice from behind the door.

619
00:23:58,958 --> 00:24:00,208
It was like a child's voice!

620
00:24:00,708 --> 00:24:01,750
It was trembling!

621
00:24:02,375 --> 00:24:04,208
He was in a really bad way!

622
00:24:04,875 --> 00:24:06,916
As if he had typhoid!

623
00:24:06,958 --> 00:24:09,125
He could barely get a word out!

624
00:24:09,666 --> 00:24:12,541
As if his head was stuck in a leopard's mouth!

625
00:24:12,750 --> 00:24:14,208
Oh, I could die!

626
00:24:14,208 --> 00:24:16,500
Look what's become of the poor young man!

627
00:24:16,583 --> 00:24:18,250
Call yourselves relatives?

628
00:24:18,291 --> 00:24:19,166
Lady Aziz!

629
00:24:19,416 --> 00:24:21,708
If I say one word to him, he'll come out!

630
00:24:21,708 --> 00:24:23,125
You've never shown him any kindness!

631
00:24:23,166 --> 00:24:24,375
Well then, I'll come and tell him

632
00:24:24,416 --> 00:24:26,041
That I forgive him!

633
00:24:26,291 --> 00:24:28,000
If you come, I'll break your leg!

634
00:24:28,500 --> 00:24:30,083
If that boy hears your gruff voice, - Lady Aziz!

635
00:24:30,083 --> 00:24:31,000
He'll be scared to death!

636
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,583
Lady Aziz!

637
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:34,458
Whatever you do, don't tell him

638
00:24:34,500 --> 00:24:36,750
That they've taken Shir-Ali to prison!

639
00:24:36,958 --> 00:24:38,416
Then there'll be no way

640
00:24:38,458 --> 00:24:39,791
To get him out of that house!

641
00:24:40,583 --> 00:24:41,666
If he finds out,

642
00:24:41,666 --> 00:24:44,541
He'll never budge from there!

643
00:25:08,708 --> 00:25:10,250
Ah! Come on kid!

644
00:25:18,833 --> 00:25:20,625
(Knocking on door)

645
00:25:40,750 --> 00:25:42,375
Whoever it is, say I'm not here!

646
00:25:51,333 --> 00:25:52,166
Who is it?

647
00:25:53,125 --> 00:25:53,875
Who is it?

648
00:25:55,166 --> 00:25:57,166
Tell Asdollah to come to the door for a minute.

649
00:25:57,958 --> 00:25:59,833
Come! They're here for you again!

650
00:25:59,875 --> 00:26:01,000
To hell with them!

651
00:26:01,041 --> 00:26:02,041
They won't leave us alone!

652
00:26:02,041 --> 00:26:02,791
Step aside.

653
00:26:02,833 --> 00:26:04,625
What do you want from me?

654
00:26:04,666 --> 00:26:06,291
I'm not coming out of this house!

655
00:26:06,375 --> 00:26:07,083
I'm scared!

656
00:26:07,125 --> 00:26:08,375
I'm scared to come out!

657
00:26:08,375 --> 00:26:08,916
Asi dear!

658
00:26:09,041 --> 00:26:10,000
Open the door.

659
00:26:10,500 --> 00:26:12,000
I want a word with you.

660
00:26:14,291 --> 00:26:16,250
No one can guarantee my safety!

661
00:26:16,625 --> 00:26:18,083
You run too, before Dustali comes!

662
00:26:18,125 --> 00:26:19,875
I said open the door!

663
00:26:20,625 --> 00:26:23,041
Dustali wouldn't dare raise a hand on you!

664
00:26:23,833 --> 00:26:25,666
I've forgiven Dustali.

665
00:26:25,958 --> 00:26:27,416
And he's forgiven us.

666
00:26:27,583 --> 00:26:29,583
Come, I'll take you, you can kiss and make up.

667
00:26:29,750 --> 00:26:30,583
Aziz dear!

668
00:26:30,833 --> 00:26:31,791
I'm scared!

669
00:26:31,833 --> 00:26:33,166
I know that Dustali,

670
00:26:33,208 --> 00:26:35,041
Is hiding behind the wall right now,

671
00:26:35,208 --> 00:26:36,916
With his dagger in his fist,

672
00:26:36,958 --> 00:26:38,833
To plunge it into my heart!

673
00:26:39,458 --> 00:26:41,000
Open the door a crack!

674
00:26:41,541 --> 00:26:43,291
See for yourself Dustali isn't here!

675
00:26:44,166 --> 00:26:45,375
Please, darling!

676
00:26:45,541 --> 00:26:46,333
Look,

677
00:26:46,375 --> 00:26:48,000
Does it look good to people,

678
00:26:48,041 --> 00:26:49,916
You alone in a house with another man's wife?

679
00:26:49,958 --> 00:26:50,583
Moment!

680
00:26:50,625 --> 00:26:51,416
Moment!

681
00:26:51,416 --> 00:26:52,833
Thank God that such slander

682
00:26:52,875 --> 00:26:54,666
Doesn't stick to me and Tahereh!

683
00:26:55,250 --> 00:26:57,166
Shir-Ali is like my brother!

684
00:26:57,833 --> 00:26:59,166
Shir-Ali's wife and children,

685
00:26:59,208 --> 00:27:01,416
Are like my own wife and children!

686
00:27:01,833 --> 00:27:03,583
Let Shir-Ali return,

687
00:27:03,833 --> 00:27:06,208
I'll hand his wife and child back to him,

688
00:27:06,541 --> 00:27:08,041
And then I'll come out!

689
00:27:08,958 --> 00:27:09,833
Asdollah!

690
00:27:09,833 --> 00:27:12,083
Shir-Ali is not coming back!

691
00:27:12,166 --> 00:27:14,791
He got in a fight, they took him to the station! Ah!

692
00:27:15,625 --> 00:27:17,416
Oh no!

693
00:27:17,666 --> 00:27:19,208
Oh, good God!

694
00:27:19,250 --> 00:27:20,833
So Shir-Ali went to prison!

695
00:27:20,916 --> 00:27:21,916
Oh my!

696
00:27:22,208 --> 00:27:22,750
No!

697
00:27:23,208 --> 00:27:23,583
No!

698
00:27:23,625 --> 00:27:24,708
Impossible!

699
00:27:24,875 --> 00:27:28,041
There's no way I'm setting foot outside this house now!

700
00:27:28,125 --> 00:27:29,708
Now it's impossible!

701
00:27:29,791 --> 00:27:30,500
Impossible!

702
00:27:30,500 --> 00:27:32,041
Impossible! I have a duty!

703
00:27:32,083 --> 00:27:32,791
Morality!

704
00:27:32,791 --> 00:27:33,750
Conscience!

705
00:27:34,500 --> 00:27:35,583
Asdollah!

706
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:37,333
I beg you, come out!

707
00:27:37,750 --> 00:27:39,916
Don't let me be humiliated in front of people!

708
00:27:44,125 --> 00:27:45,125
Lady Aziz dear...

709
00:27:45,250 --> 00:27:47,500
I'm ready to give my life for you!

710
00:27:47,875 --> 00:27:50,708
But Shir-Ali entrusted his wife and child to me!

711
00:27:50,875 --> 00:27:53,208
Shir-Ali has no children!

712
00:27:54,500 --> 00:27:55,333
Seriously?

713
00:27:55,708 --> 00:27:56,291
You don't?

714
00:27:56,666 --> 00:27:57,500
No!

715
00:27:57,958 --> 00:27:59,333
But there's his wife!

716
00:27:59,583 --> 00:28:00,875
Well, she's like a child!

717
00:28:01,500 --> 00:28:04,666
The poor thing is crying her eyes out!

718
00:28:05,875 --> 00:28:08,208
Not that I can see her face under the chador!

719
00:28:08,250 --> 00:28:09,166
I swear on your life, Lady Aziz,

720
00:28:09,208 --> 00:28:11,583
I can tell from her sobbing!

721
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:13,583
How can I let her go?

722
00:28:13,708 --> 00:28:15,125
How can I let her go?

723
00:28:15,583 --> 00:28:16,916
She says I'll be alone!

724
00:28:16,958 --> 00:28:18,875
With no one to look after me!

725
00:28:19,541 --> 00:28:23,083
If I catch that spineless jackass husband of hers,

726
00:28:23,083 --> 00:28:24,291
I'll make her a widow!

727
00:28:24,541 --> 00:28:26,041
Fine! Don't come out!

728
00:28:26,125 --> 00:28:28,166
But I'll deal with this hussy

729
00:28:28,208 --> 00:28:30,250
Who's bewitched you with her hocus-pocus!

730
00:28:30,666 --> 00:28:32,375
(Asdollah laughs quietly)

731
00:28:32,416 --> 00:28:33,500
I'll make her understand!

732
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:38,291
(They laugh)

733
00:28:42,541 --> 00:28:43,500
Wait!

734
00:28:44,833 --> 00:28:46,791
Come here, I'll look after you!

735
00:28:53,333 --> 00:28:53,875
Yes.

736
00:28:54,166 --> 00:28:54,625
Yes.

737
00:28:55,666 --> 00:28:56,375
Well...

738
00:28:56,416 --> 00:28:58,500
If that's how it is, nothing can be done!

739
00:28:58,708 --> 00:29:00,083
Much obliged, your excellency!

740
00:29:00,458 --> 00:29:01,583
The deputy commissioner says,

741
00:29:01,625 --> 00:29:03,208
Under no circumstances can he...

742
00:29:03,583 --> 00:29:04,500
You should have told them

743
00:29:04,541 --> 00:29:05,791
To release him temporarily!

744
00:29:05,791 --> 00:29:06,375
Oh dear...

745
00:29:07,166 --> 00:29:07,875
I did!

746
00:29:07,916 --> 00:29:09,000
He said it can't be done!

747
00:29:09,500 --> 00:29:13,083
They say until the dough-kneader's condition is known,

748
00:29:13,125 --> 00:29:14,750
They can't release Shir-Ali!

749
00:29:14,791 --> 00:29:16,958
This hussy has bewitched Asdollah!

750
00:29:17,166 --> 00:29:18,375
Honestly, Asdollah was never one

751
00:29:18,416 --> 00:29:19,750
To go against my word!

752
00:29:20,041 --> 00:29:20,625
We have to

753
00:29:20,833 --> 00:29:22,791
Send for Mr. Khorasani

754
00:29:22,833 --> 00:29:24,375
To bring some anti-magic vinegar

755
00:29:24,375 --> 00:29:25,458
And sprinkle it at Shir-Ali's door!

756
00:29:25,458 --> 00:29:26,500
We must do this!

757
00:29:26,541 --> 00:29:27,708
What magic?

758
00:29:27,750 --> 00:29:29,541
What's all this nonsense?

759
00:29:29,833 --> 00:29:31,458
That jackass

760
00:29:31,458 --> 00:29:32,500
Is staying there

761
00:29:32,500 --> 00:29:34,875
To fool around with Shir-Ali's wife!

762
00:29:34,916 --> 00:29:35,916
Oh, please! To hell with you!

763
00:29:35,916 --> 00:29:37,625
Asdollah would pass up decent women

764
00:29:37,625 --> 00:29:39,583
To fool around with that ugly hag?

765
00:29:39,666 --> 00:29:40,375
Get out of here!

766
00:29:40,958 --> 00:29:44,250
Stop defending this shameless thief!

767
00:29:44,791 --> 00:29:46,000
He's your brother!

768
00:29:46,041 --> 00:29:46,791
Okay!

769
00:29:46,875 --> 00:29:48,333
He's your nephew? - Enough Sir!

770
00:29:48,333 --> 00:29:49,041
Okay!

771
00:29:49,166 --> 00:29:51,708
Enough, Sir! Stop talking such nonsense!

772
00:29:52,916 --> 00:29:55,250
He's a home-wrecker!

773
00:29:55,500 --> 00:29:57,083
He's a thief, lady!

774
00:29:57,416 --> 00:29:58,750
Your Highness,

775
00:29:58,750 --> 00:30:00,166
Prince Asdollah-Mirza,

776
00:30:00,208 --> 00:30:01,791
Is a home-wrecker! - Dustali!

777
00:30:01,958 --> 00:30:02,916
I'll smack you in the mouth so hard

778
00:30:02,916 --> 00:30:04,250
Your teeth will fall out!

779
00:30:05,166 --> 00:30:06,791
When you insult my nephew,

780
00:30:06,833 --> 00:30:08,416
It's as if you're insulting me! - Quiet!

781
00:30:08,750 --> 00:30:12,166
Why don't you go fight in your own house!

782
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:14,583
What sin did I commit,

783
00:30:14,583 --> 00:30:17,208
That I have to hear this nonsense?

784
00:30:18,625 --> 00:30:21,458
Let Asdollah stay in Shir-Ali's house,

785
00:30:21,500 --> 00:30:23,458
Until he takes root there!

786
00:30:23,750 --> 00:30:25,291
What business is it of yours!

787
00:30:25,750 --> 00:30:28,125
Are you Asdollah's guardian?

788
00:30:28,125 --> 00:30:29,875
Are you trying to kill me?

789
00:30:30,083 --> 00:30:31,750
Or Shir-Ali's lawyer!

790
00:30:31,791 --> 00:30:33,541
Brother! I beg you,

791
00:30:33,541 --> 00:30:35,625
Don't get angry, calm down!

792
00:30:35,625 --> 00:30:36,666
We came here to...

793
00:30:36,708 --> 00:30:38,125
You came to do what?

794
00:30:38,291 --> 00:30:40,750
What do you want from my life?

795
00:30:41,083 --> 00:30:41,750
Brother,

796
00:30:41,791 --> 00:30:43,916
We asked you not to get angry!

797
00:30:44,083 --> 00:30:46,666
We came to resolve past differences!

798
00:30:47,083 --> 00:30:49,250
Now a more important issue has come up.

799
00:30:49,416 --> 00:30:52,166
Now the family's honor and reputation are at stake!

800
00:30:52,375 --> 00:30:53,625
No matter what,

801
00:30:53,750 --> 00:30:55,416
He must come out of Shir-Ali's house!

802
00:30:55,416 --> 00:30:56,833
I'll make Asdollah come out,

803
00:30:56,875 --> 00:30:58,583
So you can all rest easy.

804
00:30:58,875 --> 00:31:00,750
Shir-Ali's mother-in-law's house is nearby.

805
00:31:00,875 --> 00:31:01,541
I'll go there,

806
00:31:01,583 --> 00:31:03,166
Tell her to stay with her daughter so she's not alone.

807
00:31:03,166 --> 00:31:04,583
Until that bear is released from prison!

808
00:31:07,083 --> 00:31:08,958
I suggest,

809
00:31:09,291 --> 00:31:11,750
That we go visit the dough-kneader.

810
00:31:12,708 --> 00:31:14,833
They say he got hit on the head.

811
00:31:15,916 --> 00:31:17,000
Maybe the blow

812
00:31:17,333 --> 00:31:18,208
Wasn't serious!

813
00:31:18,958 --> 00:31:21,666
Maybe he's playing possum,

814
00:31:21,708 --> 00:31:23,541
To take revenge on Shir-Ali!

815
00:31:24,375 --> 00:31:25,625
If that's the case,

816
00:31:26,083 --> 00:31:28,208
We can make him some promises

817
00:31:28,416 --> 00:31:30,333
And win him over

818
00:31:30,375 --> 00:31:32,791
So he drops his complaint!

819
00:31:33,125 --> 00:31:35,291
Maybe Shir-Ali will be released today!

820
00:31:35,333 --> 00:31:36,500
A man of my position

821
00:31:36,541 --> 00:31:38,625
Should go visit a dough-kneader,

822
00:31:38,708 --> 00:31:40,875
To get him to drop charges against a butcher?!

823
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:43,458
I didn't mean you!

824
00:31:43,541 --> 00:31:44,833
One of us!

825
00:31:44,958 --> 00:31:45,583
...For example

826
00:31:45,625 --> 00:31:46,291
For example...

827
00:31:46,416 --> 00:31:48,041
One of ourselves!

828
00:31:48,500 --> 00:31:49,833
How about Mash Ghasem!

829
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:51,000
That's a good idea!

830
00:31:51,166 --> 00:31:51,916
Makes sense!

831
00:31:52,166 --> 00:31:53,625
It's not befitting our family,

832
00:31:53,666 --> 00:31:55,291
To visit a dough-kneader!

833
00:31:57,541 --> 00:31:59,541
It's much better if Mash Ghasem goes!

834
00:32:00,375 --> 00:32:01,875
I don't understand!

835
00:32:02,708 --> 00:32:05,208
Why does Shir-Ali need to be released at all!

836
00:32:05,333 --> 00:32:06,666
No reason, Sir, just because!

837
00:32:07,083 --> 00:32:08,250
Serves him right,

838
00:32:08,250 --> 00:32:10,458
He shouldn't go hitting people with lamb carcasses!

839
00:32:11,416 --> 00:32:13,875
This man has terrorized the whole neighborhood!

840
00:32:14,375 --> 00:32:16,083
Everyone is fed up with him!

841
00:32:16,750 --> 00:32:19,791
Now that the government suddenly decided to punish him,

842
00:32:19,833 --> 00:32:21,458
Why are you interfering?

843
00:32:22,833 --> 00:32:24,583
We don't care about Shir-Ali!

844
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:27,833
We are thinking of our family's reputation!

845
00:32:27,916 --> 00:32:28,458
Shir-Ali,

846
00:32:28,500 --> 00:32:29,333
Tough luck for him,

847
00:32:29,375 --> 00:32:30,208
Damn him!

848
00:32:30,250 --> 00:32:31,375
Let him rot in prison!

849
00:32:31,666 --> 00:32:33,416
We are thinking of Asdollah!

850
00:32:34,166 --> 00:32:35,500
Prince Asdollah-Mirza,

851
00:32:35,666 --> 00:32:37,916
In Shir-Ali the butcher's house!

852
00:32:39,625 --> 00:32:40,750
Tomorrow who'll be able to look

853
00:32:40,791 --> 00:32:42,791
The people of this neighborhood in the eye!

854
00:32:43,166 --> 00:32:44,500
Is it the first time,

855
00:32:44,541 --> 00:32:46,125
That Asdollah has barged into people's houses?

856
00:32:46,333 --> 00:32:47,375
Is it the first time,

857
00:32:47,375 --> 00:32:48,708
That he went to Shir-Ali's house?

858
00:32:48,958 --> 00:32:49,750
Really, gentlemen!

859
00:32:50,125 --> 00:32:52,041
Do whatever you want!

860
00:32:52,250 --> 00:32:54,041
Here's Ghasem, he's all yours!

861
00:32:54,250 --> 00:32:55,958
Send him to the grocer's,

862
00:32:55,958 --> 00:32:56,666
The rice seller's,

863
00:32:56,708 --> 00:32:57,416
The herbalist's,

864
00:32:57,458 --> 00:32:59,166
Send him to whatever hell you like!

865
00:32:59,833 --> 00:33:00,375
Gentlemen!

866
00:33:00,833 --> 00:33:02,750
Now that our brother has agreed,

867
00:33:02,791 --> 00:33:04,166
We'd better not waste time.

868
00:33:04,416 --> 00:33:05,000
Run Mash Ghasem!

869
00:33:05,125 --> 00:33:05,416
Run!

870
00:33:05,916 --> 00:33:06,750
Go on, son.

871
00:33:07,500 --> 00:33:09,041
Go see this dough-kneader.

872
00:33:09,041 --> 00:33:09,625
With money,

873
00:33:09,666 --> 00:33:11,125
Do whatever it takes

874
00:33:11,166 --> 00:33:12,916
To get him to drop his complaint.

875
00:33:12,916 --> 00:33:13,875
Go on, son... go!

876
00:33:14,250 --> 00:33:15,291
There's a problem with that.

877
00:33:15,375 --> 00:33:16,000
What problem?

878
00:33:16,583 --> 00:33:17,375
Please come.

879
00:33:18,625 --> 00:33:19,000
Huh?

880
00:33:21,375 --> 00:33:22,500
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie!

881
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:24,250
The grave is this close...

882
00:33:24,833 --> 00:33:27,083
We saw the dough-kneader an hour ago,

883
00:33:27,125 --> 00:33:29,208
His head was bandaged, they were taking him home.

884
00:33:30,416 --> 00:33:32,000
So his condition is not too bad!

885
00:33:32,458 --> 00:33:33,458
Not too bad.

886
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:35,208
But the thing is,

887
00:33:35,208 --> 00:33:37,375
We've not spoken to this dough-kneader for ten or twelve days.

888
00:33:38,333 --> 00:33:39,166
Not speaking? What do you mean?

889
00:33:40,458 --> 00:33:42,208
Sir will remember that time.

890
00:33:42,666 --> 00:33:44,583
There was a piece of sacking in the bread!

891
00:33:44,708 --> 00:33:46,333
We had a fight with the dough-kneader.

892
00:33:46,708 --> 00:33:47,958
With a scale weight,

893
00:33:48,250 --> 00:33:49,041
Pardon me...

894
00:33:50,291 --> 00:33:51,458
He hit us right here,

895
00:33:51,708 --> 00:33:53,166
And we nearly passed out!

896
00:33:53,541 --> 00:33:55,666
We whacked his head with the basket!

897
00:33:56,375 --> 00:33:57,791
They pulled us apart.

898
00:33:58,166 --> 00:33:59,916
We haven't spoken to him since that day!

899
00:34:00,708 --> 00:34:01,833
What do you mean, not speaking!

900
00:34:02,250 --> 00:34:03,583
Not speaking... means not speaking!

901
00:34:04,208 --> 00:34:04,541
Yes!

902
00:34:05,041 --> 00:34:07,750
A big man like you doesn't sulk!

903
00:34:08,541 --> 00:34:09,791
Sulking has nothing to do with size!

904
00:34:10,166 --> 00:34:10,625
Besides!

905
00:34:10,625 --> 00:34:12,541
Isn't Sir feuding with his brother-in-law?

906
00:34:12,583 --> 00:34:13,625
Don't talk nonsense!

907
00:34:14,041 --> 00:34:16,125
Honestly, Sir, we'd sooner slit our own throats

908
00:34:16,166 --> 00:34:17,833
Than spit in this dough-kneader's face!

909
00:34:17,875 --> 00:34:19,291
Let alone go and sweet-talk him!

910
00:34:19,416 --> 00:34:20,291
Mash Ghasem!

911
00:34:20,333 --> 00:34:21,708
Drop it, son!

912
00:34:21,750 --> 00:34:24,416
We Ghias-Abadis don't put up with such dishonor!

913
00:34:24,750 --> 00:34:26,250
We once had a fellow townsman,

914
00:34:26,291 --> 00:34:27,666
Not from Ghias-Abad itself!

915
00:34:27,666 --> 00:34:29,083
From the other side of Qom! - If you don't want to go, don't go!

916
00:34:29,125 --> 00:34:30,083
Don't tell stories!

917
00:34:30,250 --> 00:34:32,208
To hell with you and your fellow townsman!

918
00:34:32,666 --> 00:34:34,875
How come, Sir, you have pride and we don't?!

919
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:35,708
Ghasem!

920
00:34:36,750 --> 00:34:38,333
I command you,

921
00:34:38,375 --> 00:34:40,416
To carry out this mission.

922
00:34:41,625 --> 00:34:43,541
Just as on the battlefield

923
00:34:43,541 --> 00:34:45,000
I gave you orders,

924
00:34:45,791 --> 00:34:47,583
I'm giving you orders here!

925
00:34:48,791 --> 00:34:52,375
Imagine we're on the battlefield at Kazerun!

926
00:34:52,458 --> 00:34:53,083
Yes Sir!

927
00:34:53,083 --> 00:34:55,083
♪ Military march ♪

928
00:35:01,916 --> 00:35:05,000
(Sound of horses galloping)

929
00:35:06,166 --> 00:35:08,166
(Sound of warriors' clamor)

930
00:35:16,416 --> 00:35:18,750
Good Lord, how times have changed!

931
00:35:19,625 --> 00:35:21,333
Back then you ordered us

932
00:35:21,333 --> 00:35:23,208
To go to war with the British!

933
00:35:23,416 --> 00:35:25,333
Now we have to go to the dough-kneader!

934
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:27,875
I remember,

935
00:35:27,916 --> 00:35:30,000
In the thick of the battle of Kazerun.

936
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:31,625
We had our rifle in hand...

937
00:35:31,625 --> 00:35:33,291
Quiet Ghasem!

938
00:35:34,916 --> 00:35:35,416
Yes Sir!

939
00:35:37,333 --> 00:35:39,541
The commander gives you orders!

940
00:35:40,041 --> 00:35:40,375
Yes Sir!

941
00:35:41,791 --> 00:35:42,625
Hello. - Hello!

942
00:35:49,291 --> 00:35:49,666
Well?

943
00:35:50,875 --> 00:35:52,083
What happened Lady Aziz?

944
00:35:52,666 --> 00:35:52,958
Huh?

945
00:35:53,875 --> 00:35:56,750
Did Shir-Ali's mother-in-law go to her daughter or not?

946
00:35:57,791 --> 00:35:59,833
And she, damn her, has gone to Qom.

947
00:36:01,375 --> 00:36:05,291
♪ Calm music ♪

948
00:36:11,208 --> 00:36:12,625
Prince Asdollah-Mirza,

949
00:36:12,666 --> 00:36:13,916
Had settled comfortably in Shir-Ali the butcher's house,

950
00:36:13,958 --> 00:36:15,000
And getting him out seemed impossible.

951
00:36:15,375 --> 00:36:17,875
Uncle Napoleon was in complete despair,

952
00:36:18,375 --> 00:36:19,375
And Aqa Jan had won the war,

953
00:36:19,375 --> 00:36:20,708
On all fronts!

954
00:36:20,708 --> 00:36:22,791
♪ Cheerful traditional music ♪

955
00:36:25,041 --> 00:36:27,083
Around here,

956
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:48,666
You won't find a house this good.

957
00:36:48,708 --> 00:36:50,708
Yes!

958
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:51,625
It's sunny. Yes!

959
00:36:51,958 --> 00:36:53,041
It's sunny.

960
00:36:54,583 --> 00:36:55,000
Yes!

961
00:36:55,041 --> 00:36:55,916
OH! - Yes!

962
00:36:56,500 --> 00:36:58,875
What a lovely house Asdollah has found for us!

963
00:36:59,291 --> 00:36:59,958
The lady says,

964
00:36:59,958 --> 00:37:01,125
What a good house you found, -OH Look!

965
00:37:01,166 --> 00:37:02,583
For us, Asdollah!

966
00:37:02,875 --> 00:37:03,541
The lady is very...

967
00:37:03,541 --> 00:37:05,208
Kind. Asdollah good man

968
00:37:05,416 --> 00:37:06,791
I am known in Iran.

969
00:37:07,041 --> 00:37:08,083
Where is he now?

970
00:37:08,875 --> 00:37:10,500
Well, he's been tied up for a few days.

971
00:37:10,625 --> 00:37:11,500
He's gone to the village.

972
00:37:13,458 --> 00:37:14,333
Oh!

973
00:37:14,875 --> 00:37:16,833
Oh, look. How nice!

974
00:37:17,166 --> 00:37:18,250
Hello, kids

975
00:37:20,291 --> 00:37:20,916
Hello!

976
00:37:23,125 --> 00:37:24,000
Oh!

977
00:37:24,791 --> 00:37:26,458
Look at these kids!

978
00:37:28,166 --> 00:37:28,958
Hi!

979
00:37:31,291 --> 00:37:32,416
Hello!

980
00:37:32,416 --> 00:37:33,750
(Group laughter)

981
00:37:36,333 --> 00:37:37,041
Hello!

982
00:37:37,666 --> 00:37:38,583
Bye bye!

983
00:37:41,541 --> 00:37:43,458
Why have all these kids gathered here?

984
00:37:44,125 --> 00:37:44,708
What is he saying?

985
00:37:44,708 --> 00:37:45,500
The lady asks,

986
00:37:45,500 --> 00:37:47,125
Why have the kids gathered here?

987
00:37:47,666 --> 00:37:48,750
Nothing!

988
00:37:48,958 --> 00:37:50,041
They're locals.

989
00:37:50,083 --> 00:37:51,833
The poor things have never seen foreigners!

990
00:37:51,875 --> 00:37:52,416
Oh!

991
00:37:52,458 --> 00:37:53,458
Excuse me, sorry.

992
00:37:53,750 --> 00:37:54,666
Come on! - Go away!

993
00:37:54,708 --> 00:37:55,500
They're sweet

994
00:37:58,083 --> 00:38:00,041
You are cutie. Everyone looked at you.

995
00:38:00,083 --> 00:38:00,625
Oh!

996
00:38:02,166 --> 00:38:04,833
The local people have seen very few foreigners.

997
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:06,833
So, they are all gathered to watch you!

998
00:38:07,125 --> 00:38:08,375
The house is lovely.

999
00:38:08,625 --> 00:38:09,291
Of course,

1000
00:38:09,375 --> 00:38:10,708
The rent is not too high

1001
00:38:12,083 --> 00:38:12,666
The lady says,

1002
00:38:12,666 --> 00:38:14,333
The house is very good.

1003
00:38:14,416 --> 00:38:16,166
If the rent is not expensive.

1004
00:38:16,250 --> 00:38:18,250
Tell the lady, the rent is not important at all!

1005
00:38:18,875 --> 00:38:20,583
When are you moving in, God willing?

1006
00:38:21,208 --> 00:38:23,250
He said, The rent is not too high.

1007
00:38:23,916 --> 00:38:25,291
Could we move in tomorrow then?

1008
00:38:25,375 --> 00:38:26,083
Tomorrow good?

1009
00:38:26,625 --> 00:38:28,958
No problem, tomorrow bring the furniture here?

1010
00:38:29,375 --> 00:38:30,291
Not at all!

1011
00:38:30,291 --> 00:38:31,791
Enjoy your new home!

1012
00:38:31,916 --> 00:38:33,000
Oh! Thank you!

1013
00:38:33,708 --> 00:38:35,250
Dream on, you and that brother of yours!

1014
00:38:35,291 --> 00:38:36,375
Get lost!

1015
00:38:36,416 --> 00:38:36,791
Sir!

1016
00:38:36,791 --> 00:38:37,333
Sir!

1017
00:38:37,958 --> 00:38:38,333
He came!

1018
00:38:38,375 --> 00:38:39,333
Mash Ghasem came!

1019
00:38:40,500 --> 00:38:40,875
Yes.

1020
00:38:40,916 --> 00:38:41,375
What happened?

1021
00:38:41,708 --> 00:38:42,541
What happened Mash Ghasem?

1022
00:38:42,583 --> 00:38:42,833
What happened?

1023
00:38:42,875 --> 00:38:44,041
Honestly, Sir, why should I lie!

1024
00:38:44,083 --> 00:38:45,583
The grave is this close...

1025
00:38:45,708 --> 00:38:46,875
We didn't talk to him directly.

1026
00:38:47,083 --> 00:38:48,333
We called his brother...

1027
00:38:48,458 --> 00:38:49,750
Well, tell us what happened!

1028
00:38:50,375 --> 00:38:52,125
Back and forth, back and forth...

1029
00:38:52,166 --> 00:38:53,458
And in the end, nothing came of it!

1030
00:38:53,458 --> 00:38:54,291
What?

1031
00:38:54,375 --> 00:38:55,291
Nothing came of it?

1032
00:38:55,583 --> 00:38:57,041
Well, the dough-kneader's brother says

1033
00:38:57,083 --> 00:38:59,375
Shir-Ali has to come before all the neighborhood shopkeepers

1034
00:38:59,416 --> 00:39:00,666
And kiss the dough-kneader's hand

1035
00:39:00,666 --> 00:39:01,500
Before he'll drop the charges!

1036
00:39:03,666 --> 00:39:04,916
So this shameless guy

1037
00:39:05,041 --> 00:39:06,291
Stays in Shir-Ali's house!

1038
00:39:06,375 --> 00:39:06,958
Fine!

1039
00:39:07,000 --> 00:39:09,000
If you can, go bring him out!

1040
00:39:10,375 --> 00:39:15,000
♪ Calm music ♪

1041
00:39:21,500 --> 00:39:23,791
I came to kiss your hands and apologize.

1042
00:39:24,458 --> 00:39:25,125
Forgive me.

1043
00:39:25,166 --> 00:39:27,166
(Group murmur and happiness)

1044
00:39:27,791 --> 00:39:29,083
We knew it all along...

1045
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:33,541
God willing, may you always be at peace.

1046
00:39:33,666 --> 00:39:34,208
Congratulations!

1047
00:39:35,708 --> 00:39:37,375
Congratulations to you, God willing.

1048
00:39:37,625 --> 00:39:39,083
We told you, Sir! We knew it!

1049
00:39:39,125 --> 00:39:40,875
You are the head of our family.

1050
00:39:40,916 --> 00:39:42,916
(Group murmur and happiness)

1051
00:39:45,750 --> 00:39:47,708
♪ Traditional music ♪

1052
00:39:52,583 --> 00:39:53,250
Lily!

1053
00:39:53,875 --> 00:39:54,541
Lily!

1054
00:39:55,041 --> 00:39:55,708
Lily!

1055
00:39:56,291 --> 00:39:56,791
What is it?

1056
00:39:58,125 --> 00:39:59,875
Aqa Jan and Uncle made up!

1057
00:40:00,416 --> 00:40:01,541
Hooray!

1058
00:40:07,916 --> 00:40:08,500
Sir!

1059
00:40:10,250 --> 00:40:11,166
Here's your tea.

1060
00:40:11,208 --> 00:40:12,083
Today something happened

1061
00:40:12,083 --> 00:40:13,416
That shook me to the core!

1062
00:40:14,458 --> 00:40:16,541
I ran into a prominent public figure.

1063
00:40:16,583 --> 00:40:17,250
Well... well...

1064
00:40:17,458 --> 00:40:19,458
When the talk turned to you,

1065
00:40:19,791 --> 00:40:21,833
He said things that, believe me,

1066
00:40:21,875 --> 00:40:23,208
Really shook me!

1067
00:40:23,208 --> 00:40:23,708
Strange!

1068
00:40:23,791 --> 00:40:25,625
He said you should be proud,

1069
00:40:25,625 --> 00:40:27,833
That such a person is in your family.

1070
00:40:29,125 --> 00:40:30,958
I was telling the Prince about you.

1071
00:40:31,250 --> 00:40:31,791
Today,

1072
00:40:31,791 --> 00:40:32,500
By chance,

1073
00:40:32,500 --> 00:40:35,000
I ran into one of your old friends.

1074
00:40:35,833 --> 00:40:38,125
You can't imagine with what excitement he spoke about you!

1075
00:40:38,166 --> 00:40:38,458
He said,

1076
00:40:38,500 --> 00:40:40,458
He'd heard from Major Saxon, who during the First World War

1077
00:40:40,500 --> 00:40:42,416
Was on assignment in this country for years,

1078
00:40:42,458 --> 00:40:43,000
That,

1079
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:44,041
If it weren't for you,

1080
00:40:44,083 --> 00:40:45,333
Many things in this country

1081
00:40:45,333 --> 00:40:46,333
Would be very different now!

1082
00:40:46,708 --> 00:40:48,583
If it weren't for your struggles,

1083
00:40:48,833 --> 00:40:50,791
If it weren't for your patriotism,

1084
00:40:50,958 --> 00:40:51,458
Yes!

1085
00:40:51,458 --> 00:40:53,750
The British would have done God knows what!

1086
00:40:53,916 --> 00:40:54,291
Yes!

1087
00:40:54,291 --> 00:40:56,125
He said when you were in the south,

1088
00:40:56,208 --> 00:40:57,916
Fighting the bandits,

1089
00:40:58,041 --> 00:40:59,541
The British were ready

1090
00:40:59,541 --> 00:41:01,208
To pay a million pounds

1091
00:41:01,250 --> 00:41:02,375
To get rid of you!

1092
00:41:02,375 --> 00:41:02,833
Yes!

1093
00:41:04,541 --> 00:41:06,458
This same man praised your struggles

1094
00:41:06,500 --> 00:41:08,500
Against the supporters of despotism!

1095
00:41:09,375 --> 00:41:11,208
He said if it weren't for him,

1096
00:41:11,250 --> 00:41:12,666
There wouldn't have been a constitution at all!

1097
00:41:12,708 --> 00:41:13,416
Yes! That's right...

1098
00:41:13,583 --> 00:41:15,583
By the way... what was this man's name?

1099
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:18,541
I'm sorry, but his name...

1100
00:41:18,625 --> 00:41:19,500
I can't say it!

1101
00:41:20,500 --> 00:41:23,083
Since he told me what Major Saxon said,

1102
00:41:23,125 --> 00:41:24,333
It could be dangerous for him!

1103
00:41:24,791 --> 00:41:25,833
You know better yourself,

1104
00:41:25,833 --> 00:41:28,250
That the British show no mercy over secrets!

1105
00:41:29,541 --> 00:41:31,583
I understand... I understand.

1106
00:41:33,500 --> 00:41:34,458
Especially now that,

1107
00:41:34,500 --> 00:41:36,291
They have started such a big war!

1108
00:41:36,916 --> 00:41:39,166
Hitler drops bombs on them every night.

1109
00:41:39,666 --> 00:41:40,625
As the old saying goes,

1110
00:41:40,666 --> 00:41:42,208
The truth always comes out.

1111
00:41:42,458 --> 00:41:43,708
Sir and I know

1112
00:41:43,750 --> 00:41:46,208
What havoc Sir wreaked on the British!

1113
00:41:46,583 --> 00:41:48,125
Even now, if they let Sir loose,

1114
00:41:48,166 --> 00:41:49,875
He'd give the British hell!

1115
00:41:49,916 --> 00:41:51,041
I, for one, truly

1116
00:41:51,083 --> 00:41:53,000
Feel proud and honored!

1117
00:41:53,166 --> 00:41:53,750
Yes...

1118
00:41:53,750 --> 00:41:56,375
I'm ashamed there was a misunderstanding between us.

1119
00:41:57,041 --> 00:41:59,208
Time taught me a new lesson.

1120
00:42:01,166 --> 00:42:02,750
I swear to God I regret what I did...

1121
00:42:02,791 --> 00:42:05,000
These two are off in their fantasy world again.

1122
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:06,625
No problem...

1123
00:42:06,625 --> 00:42:09,250
Brother loves this kind of praise.

1124
00:42:09,791 --> 00:42:12,208
Now that they've made up, let them talk.

1125
00:42:13,250 --> 00:42:14,125
One more thing!

1126
00:42:14,541 --> 00:42:15,708
That same man said

1127
00:42:15,708 --> 00:42:18,583
If the British weren't busy with the war against Hitler these days,

1128
00:42:18,625 --> 00:42:20,458
They would never have left Sir alone!

1129
00:42:21,750 --> 00:42:23,666
He said in the whole of the East,

1130
00:42:23,666 --> 00:42:26,250
If anyone has foiled British plans,

1131
00:42:26,291 --> 00:42:27,291
It's Sir alone!

1132
00:42:27,291 --> 00:42:28,625
Yes... yes...

1133
00:42:29,708 --> 00:42:32,541
He said he heard it from Major Saxon's own lips

1134
00:42:32,958 --> 00:42:35,041
That only two people had ever tormented them!

1135
00:42:35,083 --> 00:42:37,500
One was Sir, in the First World War!

1136
00:42:37,541 --> 00:42:38,333
And the other was Hitler!

1137
00:42:38,375 --> 00:42:39,625
In this war they're fighting now!

1138
00:42:39,750 --> 00:42:40,666
Yes... he said it right!

1139
00:42:40,708 --> 00:42:42,791
Now think of something about Asdollah too!

1140
00:42:42,916 --> 00:42:44,083
How long is he going to stay in the house

1141
00:42:44,083 --> 00:42:46,083
Of that thick-necked thug of a butcher!

1142
00:42:46,458 --> 00:42:47,541
Dustali!

1143
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:49,416
Manners are a fine thing, you know!

1144
00:42:49,583 --> 00:42:51,458
Don't you see Sir is talking?

1145
00:42:52,916 --> 00:42:54,708
Yes, you were saying...

1146
00:42:54,875 --> 00:42:56,583
It was in the middle of the First World War

1147
00:42:56,583 --> 00:42:57,250
That the British,

1148
00:42:57,291 --> 00:42:59,958
Sent this Major Saxon to Iran.

1149
00:43:00,916 --> 00:43:01,541
Sir!

1150
00:43:01,541 --> 00:43:03,458
Isn't this the tall fellow

1151
00:43:03,458 --> 00:43:05,000
You went at with a sword?

1152
00:43:05,041 --> 00:43:06,625
The one with the cross-eyed left eye?

1153
00:43:07,583 --> 00:43:09,250
Ghasem!...

1154
00:43:10,958 --> 00:43:12,958
This person you mentioned...

1155
00:43:12,958 --> 00:43:14,208
Recently...

1156
00:43:14,791 --> 00:43:16,625
Has seen Major Saxon?

1157
00:43:16,958 --> 00:43:17,791
Yes!

1158
00:43:17,833 --> 00:43:19,291
Just two or three months ago,

1159
00:43:19,291 --> 00:43:20,708
In Istanbul.

1160
00:43:21,041 --> 00:43:23,458
Apparently he was passing through from Cairo.

1161
00:43:24,083 --> 00:43:25,291
One of these days, God willing,

1162
00:43:25,333 --> 00:43:26,666
When circumstances allow,

1163
00:43:26,666 --> 00:43:28,291
I must invite him over,

1164
00:43:28,500 --> 00:43:30,125
So you can hear from his own lips

1165
00:43:30,250 --> 00:43:32,000
What he said about you!

1166
00:43:32,833 --> 00:43:34,291
Of course, pardon me,

1167
00:43:34,500 --> 00:43:36,000
He also said plenty of nasty things!

1168
00:43:36,250 --> 00:43:37,416
He even said,

1169
00:43:37,458 --> 00:43:39,666
That you're also connected to certain other...

1170
00:43:39,916 --> 00:43:40,750
Powers.

1171
00:43:40,958 --> 00:43:41,916
Well, well!

1172
00:43:45,833 --> 00:43:48,208
It'd be strange if he'd said otherwise!

1173
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:51,375
Of course...

1174
00:43:52,208 --> 00:43:54,541
This Major Saxon's face,

1175
00:43:54,583 --> 00:43:56,791
I can't quite remember it!

1176
00:43:57,166 --> 00:43:58,708
Was he that tall one

1177
00:43:58,708 --> 00:44:01,291
We saw one day on Cheragh Bargh Street?

1178
00:44:01,791 --> 00:44:03,083
You don't remember.

1179
00:44:03,375 --> 00:44:04,250
We told you,

1180
00:44:04,291 --> 00:44:06,166
That Englishman with his crossed left eye,

1181
00:44:06,166 --> 00:44:08,250
Why is he giving you such a cross look?

1182
00:44:08,958 --> 00:44:10,958
We said right then that it looked like...

1183
00:44:11,000 --> 00:44:12,666
No Ghasem! No!

1184
00:44:13,041 --> 00:44:15,041
You're talking nonsense again!

1185
00:44:15,416 --> 00:44:17,000
Well... perhaps,

1186
00:44:17,041 --> 00:44:19,458
He was one of their agents too!

1187
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:22,291
Now, that foreigner you mention,

1188
00:44:22,291 --> 00:44:24,500
I can't quite remember his face either!

1189
00:44:25,125 --> 00:44:27,375
Sir, you may not remember,

1190
00:44:27,416 --> 00:44:28,750
But why should I lie!

1191
00:44:28,791 --> 00:44:29,708
The grave is only...

1192
00:44:30,041 --> 00:44:31,666
this far away...

1193
00:44:33,041 --> 00:44:35,666
It's as if it's right before our eyes!

1194
00:44:35,958 --> 00:44:38,250
Right then he gave Sir a look

1195
00:44:38,250 --> 00:44:39,916
That scared the life out of us!

1196
00:44:40,750 --> 00:44:42,083
Right there we said to ourselves,

1197
00:44:42,125 --> 00:44:43,333
Oh, Imam Ali!

1198
00:44:43,500 --> 00:44:46,291
Protect Sir from the evil of the British!

1199
00:44:47,375 --> 00:44:50,750
Everything we did for the homeland,

1200
00:44:50,791 --> 00:44:51,833
Was our duty.

1201
00:44:52,208 --> 00:44:54,833
We weren't afraid of the consequences.

1202
00:44:55,666 --> 00:44:57,583
Do you think,

1203
00:44:57,833 --> 00:44:59,833
I didn't know what,

1204
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:02,666
Fighting the British meant?

1205
00:45:03,250 --> 00:45:05,916
Do you think I was unaware?

1206
00:45:06,000 --> 00:45:09,833
Didn't I know they'd hold back my career?

1207
00:45:10,166 --> 00:45:11,041
Of course!

1208
00:45:11,375 --> 00:45:12,583
I knew!

1209
00:45:13,916 --> 00:45:19,458
I braced myself for every kind of humiliation and misery and...

1210
00:45:19,458 --> 00:45:21,166
I fought!

1211
00:45:22,041 --> 00:45:24,875
So many go-betweens they sent...

1212
00:45:25,541 --> 00:45:28,208
How many people they sent...

1213
00:45:28,458 --> 00:45:29,208
Never mind!

1214
00:45:29,958 --> 00:45:31,416
They made threats!

1215
00:45:31,583 --> 00:45:33,083
They offered bribes!

1216
00:45:33,291 --> 00:45:34,333
I remember,

1217
00:45:34,583 --> 00:45:37,666
On my last posting in Mashhad,

1218
00:45:38,791 --> 00:45:40,541
It was around sunset...

1219
00:45:40,625 --> 00:45:42,541
I was going home.

1220
00:45:43,750 --> 00:45:44,541
Perhaps...

1221
00:45:45,166 --> 00:45:47,625
Perhaps this Ghasem was with me!

1222
00:45:48,583 --> 00:45:50,375
Yes Sir! We were there.

1223
00:45:50,750 --> 00:45:51,416
Yes.

1224
00:45:52,708 --> 00:45:55,625
As we were walking along,

1225
00:45:56,458 --> 00:46:00,375
Suddenly I saw an Indian-looking man,

1226
00:46:00,875 --> 00:46:04,875
Following me like a shadow!

1227
00:46:05,416 --> 00:46:08,250
I paid no attention at all!

1228
00:46:09,541 --> 00:46:10,250
Then,

1229
00:46:10,833 --> 00:46:12,500
Early that evening,

1230
00:46:12,708 --> 00:46:15,416
I was at home, there was a knock!

1231
00:46:15,875 --> 00:46:18,625
My servant went to the door!

1232
00:46:18,708 --> 00:46:20,125
That was us!

1233
00:46:21,000 --> 00:46:22,166
Y... yes, yes!

1234
00:46:22,208 --> 00:46:24,416
Ghasem went to the door and... - Yes! We were there!

1235
00:46:24,458 --> 00:46:25,583
He came back and said,

1236
00:46:25,875 --> 00:46:26,708
Sir!

1237
00:46:27,291 --> 00:46:29,500
An Indian has come,

1238
00:46:29,791 --> 00:46:31,791
He says he's a pilgrim,

1239
00:46:32,083 --> 00:46:34,833
Something bad has happened to him,

1240
00:46:35,083 --> 00:46:38,083
He wants a few words with Sir!

1241
00:46:38,875 --> 00:46:41,958
I knew at once

1242
00:46:42,375 --> 00:46:44,833
That he was one of their agents!

1243
00:46:45,416 --> 00:46:46,875
I went behind the door,

1244
00:46:47,083 --> 00:46:48,666
I swear on Lily's life...

1245
00:46:49,291 --> 00:46:51,375
I shouted,

1246
00:46:51,791 --> 00:46:53,333
Tell this man

1247
00:46:53,375 --> 00:46:55,375
Over my dead body!

1248
00:46:55,416 --> 00:46:57,416
God bless, Sir has the heart of a lion!

1249
00:46:57,875 --> 00:46:59,500
I wouldn't even agree

1250
00:46:59,666 --> 00:47:01,666
To exchange one word with him!

1251
00:47:02,333 --> 00:47:03,166
Isn't that right Ghasem?

1252
00:47:03,208 --> 00:47:05,125
Yes! We remember well!

1253
00:47:05,458 --> 00:47:06,958
As soon as Sir said this,

1254
00:47:06,958 --> 00:47:08,416
We closed the door so hard,

1255
00:47:08,458 --> 00:47:10,750
His turban flew three yards!

1256
00:47:11,375 --> 00:47:12,750
What a shame you weren't there to see,

1257
00:47:12,791 --> 00:47:14,958
What curses Sir hurled at that Indian!

1258
00:47:15,083 --> 00:47:17,041
You can't imagine how Sir humiliated him!

1259
00:47:17,500 --> 00:47:20,083
I sent him packing in disgrace!

1260
00:47:21,083 --> 00:47:22,500
I said go,

1261
00:47:23,250 --> 00:47:25,666
Go tell your master,

1262
00:47:26,458 --> 00:47:28,916
So-and-so is not for sale!

1263
00:47:29,500 --> 00:47:31,708
The Indian wanted to say something to Sir,

1264
00:47:31,708 --> 00:47:33,208
But Sir wouldn't let him!

1265
00:47:33,208 --> 00:47:35,166
He ordered us to close the door on him!

1266
00:47:35,916 --> 00:47:38,666
That Indian gave us a look as he left

1267
00:47:38,666 --> 00:47:40,041
That sent a shiver down our spine!

1268
00:47:40,583 --> 00:47:42,333
His eyes in the middle of his black face,

1269
00:47:42,375 --> 00:47:43,875
Were like a cat's eyes!

1270
00:47:44,333 --> 00:47:45,708
Right there we said to ourselves,

1271
00:47:45,708 --> 00:47:47,083
Oh, Imam Ali!

1272
00:47:47,333 --> 00:47:49,916
Protect Sir yourself from the evil of the British!

1273
00:47:49,916 --> 00:47:51,083
Ghasem!

1274
00:47:51,541 --> 00:47:51,916
Yes.

1275
00:47:52,291 --> 00:47:53,250
Enough.

1276
00:47:55,500 --> 00:47:58,125
But today you can walk with your head held high!

1277
00:47:58,333 --> 00:48:00,708
A whole family is proud of you.

1278
00:48:01,791 --> 00:48:02,875
I say, how about

1279
00:48:03,000 --> 00:48:04,458
A round of backgammon?

1280
00:48:04,500 --> 00:48:05,375
Excellent!

1281
00:48:05,375 --> 00:48:07,541
Ghasem, hurry up and bring that backgammon board!

1282
00:48:07,541 --> 00:48:08,125
Yes Sir!

1283
00:48:10,083 --> 00:48:11,500
If this family,

1284
00:48:11,541 --> 00:48:13,333
Has any honor and dignity,

1285
00:48:13,541 --> 00:48:16,083
It shouldn't let itself be stained with shame.

1286
00:48:16,250 --> 00:48:18,041
Right now a member of this family

1287
00:48:18,083 --> 00:48:20,208
Is in a knife-wielding butcher's house!

1288
00:48:20,208 --> 00:48:21,708
And no one is thinking about it!

1289
00:48:21,875 --> 00:48:23,291
Mr. Dustali Khan!

1290
00:48:23,333 --> 00:48:26,041
That's enough, shame on you!

1291
00:48:26,583 --> 00:48:29,375
Stop making snide remarks about my brother!

1292
00:48:29,666 --> 00:48:31,500
The poor thing, out of fear of you,

1293
00:48:31,541 --> 00:48:32,833
Has taken refuge with the butcher.

1294
00:48:33,166 --> 00:48:35,958
If your heart's aching for the butcher's wife,

1295
00:48:36,000 --> 00:48:37,750
That's a different story!

1296
00:48:37,750 --> 00:48:39,666
To hell with her and her aching heart!

1297
00:48:39,708 --> 00:48:40,833
If one more time,

1298
00:48:40,875 --> 00:48:42,375
You talk nonsense behind my nephew's back,

1299
00:48:42,416 --> 00:48:43,833
I'll knock your teeth down your throat!

1300
00:48:44,125 --> 00:48:45,750
I talked to Asdollah!

1301
00:48:45,958 --> 00:48:47,208
The poor thing is upset

1302
00:48:47,250 --> 00:48:49,625
About leaving Shir-Ali's wife and child unprotected.

1303
00:48:49,625 --> 00:48:52,000
Oh, come off it! Shir-Ali has no children!

1304
00:48:52,541 --> 00:48:54,750
Well, his wife is like a child too.

1305
00:48:54,791 --> 00:48:56,708
Asdollah is a very sensitive person!

1306
00:48:56,750 --> 00:48:58,875
Who cares if he's sensitive!

1307
00:48:58,916 --> 00:49:00,000
Oh, get lost, you too...

1308
00:49:00,041 --> 00:49:00,625
Dustali!

1309
00:49:00,750 --> 00:49:02,208
Dustali, wait, I want a word with you! - Oh, drop it!

1310
00:49:02,333 --> 00:49:03,000
Wait! - Lady Aziz,

1311
00:49:03,041 --> 00:49:04,916
You shouldn't tease Dustali so much either.

1312
00:49:04,958 --> 00:49:06,000
That'll teach him to meddle!

1313
00:49:06,041 --> 00:49:06,750
But it wasn't nice, - Calm down!

1314
00:49:06,750 --> 00:49:08,750
You always humiliate him in front of others!

1315
00:49:08,791 --> 00:49:09,541
I can't stand it,

1316
00:49:09,541 --> 00:49:11,333
When someone disrespects my nephew!

1317
00:49:11,375 --> 00:49:12,625
This poor guy didn't say anything!

1318
00:49:12,625 --> 00:49:13,500
Come, come, come!

1319
00:49:13,541 --> 00:49:14,458
Honestly,

1320
00:49:14,458 --> 00:49:15,625
The poor thing didn't say anything bad!

1321
00:49:15,666 --> 00:49:16,208
Brother!

1322
00:49:17,250 --> 00:49:18,958
I want to ask everyone,

1323
00:49:18,958 --> 00:49:21,250
To celebrate the end of the misunderstanding,

1324
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:24,541
Everyone come to our house for dinner!

1325
00:49:24,583 --> 00:49:25,333
Bravo!

1326
00:49:25,625 --> 00:49:27,625
I want to give everyone some of that 20-year-old wine!

1327
00:49:27,666 --> 00:49:28,750
Bravo!

1328
00:49:28,791 --> 00:49:29,791
Here's to the colonel and his wines!

1329
00:49:30,208 --> 00:49:33,125
(Toasting, everyone laughs and claps)

1330
00:49:33,375 --> 00:49:34,625
For God's sake, gentlemen, be careful,

1331
00:49:34,666 --> 00:49:36,208
Let's not have any more noises,

1332
00:49:36,250 --> 00:49:36,958
Because just one of them

1333
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:38,750
Was enough to last us seven generations!

1334
00:49:38,791 --> 00:49:40,458
(Group laughter)

1335
00:49:40,458 --> 00:49:44,000
♪ Ride of the valkyrie ♪

